obj.show();', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Polymorphism', 'B', 'The reference type is A but the object is a B. The overridden method is chosen at run time, so B.show() runs.'),
(187, 7, NULL, 'Overload Resolution', 'A class has two methods: void f(int x) and void f(long x). Which is called by f(5)?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Polymorphism', 'f(int x)', 'The literal 5 is an int, so the exact match f(int) is preferred over a widening conversion to long.'),
(188, 7, NULL, 'Immutable Class Example', 'Which of the following Java classes is immutable?', 'EASY', 'MCQ', 'Java Basics', 'String', 'Once created, a String''s contents cannot change. Methods like concat return a new String.'),
(189, 7, NULL, 'equals() and hashCode() Contract', 'If two objects are equal according to equals(), what must be true about their hashCode() values?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Java Basics', 'They must be equal', 'The contract requires equal objects to have equal hash codes. Otherwise hash-based collections like HashMap break.'),
(190, 7, NULL, 'Upcasting', 'Assigning a subclass object to a superclass reference variable is called:', 'EASY', 'MCQ', 'Polymorphism', 'Upcasting', 'Upcasting is implicit and always safe. Downcasting needs an explicit cast and can fail at run time.'),
(191, 7, NULL, 'protected Access', 'Which Java access modifier allows access within the same package and also from subclasses in other packages?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Access Modifiers', 'protected', 'protected members are visible in the package and to subclasses. Package-private is visible only inside the package.'),
(192, 7, NULL, 'Instantiating an Abstract Class', 'Can you create an object of an abstract class directly using new?', 'EASY', 'MCQ', 'Abstraction', 'No, only of a concrete subclass', 'Abstract classes are incomplete by design. You instantiate a concrete subclass instead.'),
(193, 7, NULL, 'Virtual Destructors in C++', 'Why should a base class that is used polymorphically have a virtual destructor in C++?', 'HARD', 'MCQ', 'Polymorphism', 'So deleting a derived object through a base pointer calls the derived destructor', 'Without a virtual destructor, deleting through a base pointer is undefined behaviour and the derived part may not be destroyed properly (leaks).'),
(194, 7, NULL, 'Cohesion and Coupling', 'Which combination do good object-oriented designs aim for?', 'EASY', 'MCQ', 'Design Principles', 'High cohesion and low coupling', 'Classes should be focused (high cohesion) and depend on each other as little as possible (low coupling).'),
(195, 7, NULL, 'Static Method Hiding', 'A subclass declares a static method with the same signature as a static method in its superclass. What is this called?', 'HARD', 'MCQ', 'Inheritance', 'Method hiding (it is not overriding)', 'Static methods are bound to the class, so the subclass method hides the parent''s one. The choice depends on the reference type, not the object.'),
(196, 7, NULL, 'Marker Interface', 'Which of these is a marker interface in Java (an interface with no methods)?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Java Basics', 'Serializable', 'Serializable has no methods. It only marks that a class''s objects can be serialized.'),
(197, 6, NULL, 'ARP - Mapping IP to MAC', 'Which protocol is used to find the MAC address that belongs to a known IP address on a local network?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Address Resolution', 'ARP', 'The Address Resolution Protocol broadcasts a request and the owner of the IP replies with its MAC address.'),
(198, 6, NULL, 'DHCP - Automatic Configuration', 'What does DHCP do?', 'EASY', 'MCQ', 'DHCP', 'Automatically assigns IP addresses and network settings to devices', 'A DHCP server leases an IP address, subnet mask, gateway and DNS server to each client.'),
(199, 6, NULL, 'Subnet Mask for a /26 Network', 'Which subnet mask corresponds to the prefix length /26?', 'HARD', 'MCQ', 'Subnetting', '255.255.255.192', '26 bits are 1s: 255.255.255.11000000, and 11000000 in binary is 192.'),
(200, 6, NULL, 'NAT - Private to Public Translation', 'What is the main purpose of Network Address Translation (NAT)?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'NAT', 'To let devices with private IP addresses share a public IP address', 'NAT rewrites source addresses and ports so many internal hosts can reach the internet through one public address.'),
(201, 6, NULL, 'HTTP 429 Status Code', 'Which HTTP status code tells a client it has sent too many requests (rate limiting)?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'HTTP', '429 Too Many Requests', '429 is returned when a client exceeds a rate limit and often includes a Retry-After header.'),
(202, 6, NULL, 'Switch vs Hub', 'Which device forwards frames using MAC addresses at the data link layer?', 'EASY', 'MCQ', 'Network Devices', 'Switch', 'A switch learns which MAC address is on which port and forwards frames only to the right port. A hub repeats traffic to every port.'),
(203, 6, NULL, 'TLS - What It Provides', 'Which set of guarantees does TLS provide for a connection?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Security', 'Encryption, authentication of the server and message integrity', 'TLS encrypts traffic, authenticates the server with a certificate, and detects tampering.'),
(204, 6, NULL, 'Distance-Vector Routing Protocol', 'Which of the following is a distance-vector routing protocol?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Routing', 'RIP', 'RIP shares its routing table with neighbours and uses hop count. OSPF and IS-IS are link-state protocols.'),
(205, 6, NULL, 'ICMP - Ping', 'Which protocol does the ping command use to test reachability?', 'EASY', 'MCQ', 'ICMP', 'ICMP', 'Ping sends ICMP Echo Request messages and waits for Echo Replies.'),
(206, 6, NULL, 'Idempotent HTTP Methods', 'Which HTTP method is idempotent, meaning repeating the same request has the same effect as sending it once?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'HTTP', 'PUT', 'PUT replaces a resource with the given representation, so repeating it leaves the same result. POST usually creates a new resource each time, and PATCH is not guaranteed to be idempotent.'),
(207, 6, NULL, 'IMAP vs POP3', 'How does IMAP differ from POP3?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Email Protocols', 'IMAP keeps messages on the server and syncs them across devices', 'POP3 typically downloads and removes mail from the server, while IMAP leaves it there. SMTP is used to send mail.'),
(208, 6, NULL, 'WebSocket vs HTTP', 'What is the main advantage of a WebSocket connection over repeated HTTP requests for a chat application?', 'MEDIUM', 'MCQ', 'Application Layer', 'A persistent full-duplex connection so the server can push messages', 'After the upgrade handshake, client and server can send messages at any time over one connection.');



